# The full gate, once, before anything leaves the machine.
#
# Deliberately not on pre-commit: it runs every suite plus the coverage thresholds, which is far
# too slow to pay on each commit and would train everyone to reach for --no-verify. Here it is
# paid once per push and catches what pre-commit cannot — a rule whose test was never written, a
# threshold that stopped being met, a coverage ratchet that has fallen behind.
#
# The suites needing a running stack (integration, E2E) are not here: they need `supabase start`
# and a built app, so they belong to CI and to a deliberate local run.
pnpm verify
